I'm not sure if it is safe/correct to static_cast a unique_ptr<MockGpio> to a MockGpio* and then wrap that in another unique_ptr. I worry about both objects trying to delete the same memory. Maybe you already checked into this. It just looks pretty complex.

Can you instead do the following?
```
mockGpios.emplace_back(static_cast<std::unique_ptr<MockGpio>>(services.createGPIO(...)));
```

Another option is to write a helper function like
```
MockGpio& getMockGpio(Chassis& chassis, int i)
{
  return static_cast<MockGpio&>(*(chassis.getGpios()[i]));
}
```

This would allow you to create all the objects, move them into the Chassis, and then make the EXPECT_CALLs before the monitor().

```
EXPECT_CALL(getMockGpio(chassis, 0), ...);
```

Sorry I didn't try to compile any of that code. There are probably some bugs. Just trying to get a general idea.
